   "text": [
    {
     "id": "editorial",
     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "S2 · ARGUED · M39",
     "title": "S2 — AIKit: potency",
     "italic": "MEF pair L2 Logical × L3′ Chronological · movement M39 · parent S",
     "body": "",
     "x": 0.033,
     "y": 0.04,
     "width": 440,
     "size": 25,
     "align": "left"
    },
    {
     "id": "body",
     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "",
     "title": "",
     "italic": "",
     "body": "AIKit is potency: the changing horizon of what a Life can know, express, reach and bring to bear. Capacity in this sense is not an inventory of tools. A capacity may exist yet be unavailable here; available yet irrelevant; relevant yet forbidden; permitted yet unselected; selected yet unable to become operative.",
     "x": 0.57,
     "y": 0.06,
     "width": 430,
     "size": 14,
     "align": "left"
    },
    {
     "id": "lens1",
     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "L2 Logical: capacity includes absence, ambiguity and silence",
     "title": "",
     "italic": "",
     "body": "The Logical lens gives tetralemmaic ground · IS · IS-NOT · BOTH · NEITHER · SILENCE. IS names what is presently available as an operative determination. IS-NOT names what is excluded or unavailable under the current conditions. BOTH keeps co-presence where two capacities genuinely apply together. NEITHER holds a case current distinctions do not yet decide. SILENCE preserves the possibility that the right operation is not yet articulation.",
     "x": 0.033,
     "y": 0.57,
     "width": 390,
     "size": 14,
     "align": "left"
    },
    {
     "id": "lens2",
     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "L3′ Chronological: powers arise, mature, recede and return",
     "title": "",
     "italic": "",
     "body": "A power can first be latent as Spirit, enter emergence in Spring, become readily operative in Summer, pass into evaluation and harvesting in Autumn, recede or become unavailable in Winter, and be retained or transformed within a new whole as Life/Aufhebung. The pair makes temporality internal to what capacity means; development can require relinquishment.",
     "x": 0.51,
     "y": 0.57,
     "width": 400,
     "size": 14,
     "align": "left"
    }
   ],
